{
  "id": "Compound::DB01583 - Gene::7067",
  "verbalization": "Liotrix is implicated in the pathogenesis of multiple skeletal disorders, including Craniosynostosis, Slipped Femoral Capital Epiphysis, and Epiphysiolysis, all of which are linked to Dextrothyroxine. These conditions are mediated through a common pathway involving Dextrothyroxine, which binds to Thra, suggesting a potential role for Liotrix in modulating Thra activity. The shared lowest common ancestors—Thyroid Agent and Phenylalanine Derivative—highlight a broader biological context where Dextrothyroxine interacts with Thra, possibly through a conserved mechanism. The evidence supports a direct or indirect relationship between Liotrix and Thra, likely through Dextrothyroxine, which acts as a bridge in the pathophysiological process. The integration of these pathways underscores a possible dependency on thyroid-related molecules, reinforcing the notion that Liotrix may influence Thra through a mechanism involving Dextrothyroxine.",
